# Sub-tick interpolation of the gem-glint stars (scripts/check_glint_subtick.sh).
#   <bk2> | <V> | gem=<x>,<y> rec=<addr> ... [tol=<px>] [step=<px>]
# V is the tick whose primitives the intermediate present at V+1 replays; V-2
# opens the interval that present covers. Each gem is named by its mask
# component's centroid in the canonical capture at V, and must be unoccluded
# over the interval: a partly covered star's visible centroid measures the
# depth test rather than the rebase. Each gem's rec= names the pool record
# whose traced outline centroid is judged (PSX px); the mask centroid is
# reported only, since a rotating star's mask centroid traces an arc.
#
# The camera moves 24-29 PSX px per tick over this portal entry, 29.8 px on the
# 640-wide capture. The other two crosses in view, near (121.5,69.0) and
# (587.4,130.2), are partly covered by the terrain the camera passes and are
# reported, not judged.
# The gem is far cross 80067D00. Mask centroid at alpha 0.5, capture px: 0.29
# with the replay rotating against the routine's sense, 0.35 with its sense.
# Geometric centroid at alpha 0.5, PSX px: 0.075 before, 0.050 after (alpha 0
# 0.350 before, 0.255 after, the cross's extent no longer scaled by view-Z);
# identity 0.000.
autumn-plains-skelos-badlands-portal-entry.bk2 | 850 | gem=512.3,138.8 rec=80067D00 tol=0.5 step=10
